{
  "id": "exposure-and-response-prevention",
  "term": "exposure and response prevention",
  "definition": "Exposure and response prevention is a psychological treatment for obsessive compulsive disorder in which a person practices exposure exercises while refraining from the usual response-prevention behaviors that maintain the problem. It is considered a first-line treatment, and its benefit depends in part on carrying out the exposure and response-prevention work as prescribed, including between sessions.",
